            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Legacy in Law and Politics</strong><br>\nCicero's influence on law and politics extends beyond his lifetime. His legal philosophy emphasized natural law and the rights of citizens, precepts that influenced European and American legal thought. His ideas are echoed in many democratic traditions, underlining the rule of law and the importance of public service.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Impact on the Latin Language</strong><br>\nCicero's writings are among the greatest examples of classical Latin. His style shaped the Latin language, and his works were used to teach Latin for centuries. Through his writings, Cicero set the standard for Latin prose, affecting the way the language was written and spoken.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Cicero in Literature and Media</strong><br>\nOver time, Cicero has been a subject of interest in literature and media. His life and work have inspired plays, novels, and films, portraying him as a symbol of civic virtue and the complexities of politics. His quotations continue to be cited in discussions of ethics, politics, and law.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
